          "description_hash": "sha256:b649587560b18e7e00c91040f3860e51f09e343500f4b2e0e67f74ef340d7a04"
        },
        {
          "name": "trace",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:d9eeb6283a7abf2d0b387fc1a9daf6e22f1652a30f56ec15287cad5bcf64dca6",
          "description": "Follow the code across boundaries. One argument: trace a feature end-to-end — the ordered path from entry through the stack, each hop labelled with its mechanism (call / HTTP / queue / event / data), crossing service boundaries (frontend→backend). Two arguments: the shortest path between two specific nodes, hop by hop. This is where the graph beats reading many files — it knows the cross-stack links grep can't see.",
          "is_mutating": false,
